e":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Enumerate the drain() consumers outside src/rebar/llm (tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py and tests/unit/test_spawn_detached.py) and confirm the new concurrency guard + batch clamp leave their assertions (e.g. result['processed']==1) green, or list required updates.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.425,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Scope lists only 'tests/unit/test_enrich_drain.py' among test files","enrich_drain.drain(...) called at tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py:1750,1794,1795 with 'assert result_a[\"processed\"] == 1'","enrich_drain.drain invoked via re-entry stub at tests/unit/test_spawn_detached.py:118","The new concurrency guard returns {'skipped':'concurrency-cap'} when >=3 live-lease drainer_ids exist, altering drain()'s early-return surface"],"finding":"The plan's Scope enumerates only tests/unit/test_enrich_drain.py for test updates, but drain() has consumers outside the artifact directory that the restructure could affect: tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py (three call sites, asserting result['processed']==1) and tests/unit/test_spawn_detached.py (drain re-entry stub). The 'processed' summary key is preserved so those assertions likely hold, but the new concurrency guard and lease-derived batch clamp are unacknowledged interactions with these sequential/planted-claim integration drains.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc9ec2a11d670d361","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope section (test enumeration); tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py:1750,1794-1797","norm_id":"n7ba57b64f136dade","priority":0.275,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An integration drain that plants/leaves live-lease claims trips the new concurrency-cap guard and returns a skip dict lacking 'processed', failing the existing assertion","The batch clamp changes effective batch for a test that implicitly relied on batch=5 default"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State whether the 40s per-item divisor is intentionally hardcoded (with rationale) or should be a named constant/config; document its provenance and the consequence if per-item latency exceeds it.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T5e"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'40s is the worst-case per-item budget for the trivial-class digest call' — asserted, not derived from measurement in the plan","If digest LLM latency rises, the clamp under/over-sizes the batch relative to lease safety"],"finding":"The 40s per-item worst-case budget in the clamp formula `max(1, lease_ttl_s // 40)` is a hardcoded magic divisor with no configurability, despite being an asserted latency assumption that may evolve.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0da6cd4533619c98","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach ('clamp the effective per-run batch to a lease-derived bound `max(1, lease_ttl_s // 40)`')","norm_id":"n5397ab44d6721c3b","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Provider latency changes and the 40s assumption no longer holds; the batch outruns the lease mid-run — the exact failure the clamp exists to prevent"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Extract 40 to a named module constant (e.g. WORST_CASE_PER_ITEM_S = 40) with a comment tying it to the measured trivial-class digest latency, so its assumption is visible and revisable.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify which read the FINALIZE emit keys its content_hash to: hash and emit against the SAME state enrich() consumed (or re-run the content-hash from enrich's returned/echoed state), so the stored content_hash cannot disagree with the digest content when the collect/finalize hashes happen to match.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'FINALIZE ... re-read the ticket; if its content hash changed since collect -> skip the emit and re-enqueue ... else ds.emit (with the revalidated state) + mark_done.'","enrich.py:170 shows enrich(ticket_id=...) does its OWN _reads.show_ticket at ENRICH time (call it S1) and builds the digest from S1; the plan's guard compares the COLLECT snapshot hash (H0) against a FINALIZE re-read (H2), never against S1.","digest_sidecar.build_payload keys the stored record on content_hash(state) of whatever state is passed to emit — so 'with the revalidated state' hashes S2, not S1."],"finding":"The FINALIZE revalidation keys the emitted digest's content_hash to a different ticket read than the one enrich() computed the digest from, so a collect->enrich edit that reverts by finalize can store a digest whose content and content_hash disagree.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff60829ddbec48c6a","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach -> FINALIZE phase; cross-ref src/rebar/llm/enrich.py:170 and src/rebar/llm/overlap/digest_sidecar.py:emit/build_payload","norm_id":"n44daf925c6b32cab","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A ticket edited after COLLECT's snapshot but before enrich()'s internal read, then edited back (or to the same normalized text) before FINALIZE: H0==H2 passes the guard, but the digest reflects the transient S1 content and is stored under S2's hash — a digest that reads present-fresh yet describes content the ticket no longer has."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Have enrich() return (or the drain capture) the exact state it summarized, and pass that state to ds.emit so build_payload's content_hash is computed over the same bytes the digest was derived from; keep the H0-vs-H2 collect/finalize guard purely as the 'skip + re-enqueue soak 0' staleness gate.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.6667,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the back-out plan for the drain restructure (e.g. `REBAR_LLM_OVERLAP_DRAIN=off` disables the concurrent path, or a clean git revert of the single-file change), and note it explicitly as the reversibility mechanism.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T4"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'behavior-preserving extraction along the existing call-graph seams' is claimed but the lock-hold and batch semantics demonstrably change","UNCHANGED list preserves the env door meaning but does not describe a back-out path for the restructure itself"],"finding":"The plan restructures the drain lock/job-queue semantics (a structural behavior change) but names no explicit rollback/back-out mechanism beyond implicit revert; the only escape hatch (REBAR_LLM_OVERLAP_DRAIN=off) disables overlap drain entirely rather than reverting to the old single-flight-under-lock behavior.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe5f6d32584504c8a","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope / Approach (drain() split into collect/enrich/finalize)","norm_id":"ndfe7e5aa603b2bfa","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Production regression in the new three-phase flow (e.g. claim arbitration bug) with no documented way to fall back to the prior behavior short of a full revert"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a one-line rollback note: the change is confined to enrich_drain.py + one config default, so `git revert` restores prior behavior, and REBAR_LLM_OVERLAP_DRAIN=off disables overlap drain in the interim.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name the 40s worst-case-per-item divisor as a module-level constant co-located with DEFAULT_OVERLAP_DRAIN_BATCH (with a one-line rationale tying it to the trivial-class digest budget), so the batch default and the lease-derived clamp bound are visibly coherent and the divisor is not a buried magic number.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'clamp the effective per-run batch to a lease-derived bound max(1, lease_ttl_s // 40) (= 22 at the default 15-min lease ... 40s is the worst-case per-item budget for the trivial-class digest call)'","config.py has DEFAULT_OVERLAP_LEASE_TTL_MIN=15 and DEFAULT_OVERLAP_DRAIN_BATCH; the 40 has no existing named home","This is a coherence/coupling note, not a rebuild: no existing lease->batch helper exists to reuse (grep for lease_ttl found only claim() and the config field)"],"finding":"The lease-derived clamp introduces a hardcoded magic divisor (40s worst-case per-item budget) that coexists with the config default DEFAULT_OVERLAP_DRAIN_BATCH=20; the two constants must stay mutually coherent, and because the clamp is lease-derived, an operator changing REBAR_LLM_OVERLAP_LEASE_TTL_MIN silently reshapes the effective batch cap through a constant they cannot see.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6e2e801fff6e05f9","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'clamp the effective per-run batch to a lease-derived bound max(1, lease_ttl_s // 40)'; Scope — config.py DEFAULT_OVERLAP_DRAIN_BATCH 5->20","norm_id":"n6e41de8a4c6d4cd3","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An operator raises the lease TTL for slow providers and the effective batch silently grows beyond the operator's ~20-25 window","A future change to the digest op's per-item time makes 40 wrong, but the constant is buried in drain() rather than named beside the batch default"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Define e.g. DEFAULT_OVERLAP_DRAIN_WORST_ITEM_S = 40 in config.py next to DEF